      "summary": "Skiing is possible today, with Cardrona open and a fresh 10 cm of overnight snow producing soft new snow over a firmer base. The resort is reporting fresh snow affected by some wind, with dust-on-crust concerns in places, while groomed areas have been prepared with softer, more forgiving cord. At -6°C with 18 km/h winds and gusts to 32 km/h, conditions are firmly wintry; the forecast calls for a fine day as any morning cloud clears. McDougall’s Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow’s Quad are open, along with Kindy Conveyor and Learner Conveyors. Wells Pipe Platter is closed. Main Basin and Valley View were scheduled from 8:30am, with Captains, Willows, Soho and T-Bar following from 9:00am; Soho opened at 11:00am and Willows at 11:07am. Learners Slopes, Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Ski Touring Access, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and Summit are open. (Issued: 11:07am, 10 Sep) Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks, Peoples Pipe and Gravity Cross are open, while Olympic Pipe and Big Air are closed. Access roads are chain free, but chains must be carried, with an active road hazard advisory. Carpark A is full, while Carparks B and C, The Yard, Valley View and The Pines are available. The resort expects another busy day and is asking guests to carpool where possible. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 9 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
