      "summary": "Skiing is possible today, with Treble Cone open and 10 cm of dry overnight snow providing fresh terrain across Home Basin, Saddle Basin and the Summit Slopes. The resort reports some drifts off trail, stripped areas and dust-on-crust, while groomed cord should be soft and forgiving. It is currently -4°C with 14 km/h winds and 24 km/h gusts, with a fine day forecast. Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter are open. Triple Treat, Main Street, Roller Coaster, Beginner Platter, Raffil's Run, Bullet, Pete's Treat and High Street are open. Home Basin, Powder Bowl, Matukituki Basin, Saddle Basin, Summit Slopes, Backcountry Access and Skinning Access are open; Motatapu Chutes is on hold. (Issued: 10:00am, 10 Sep) The access road is chain free, but all vehicles must carry chains; the road is narrow in places and a free shuttle operates from the bottom of the access road. Home Basin and Saddle Basin are open. Treble Cone’s carparks are all available, and the resort reports a fine forecast with the mountain offering fresh snow in the sun. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 3 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
